course: dictionary
lesson: 4955
title: Inactive: not moving, working or in use
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inactive is built from in- (not) and active (doing things), so it means not active: not moving, working or doing anything. «The volcano is inactive, so it is not erupting today.» The clue is «not erupting», so inactive means quiet and still, not busy.
explain: The word can describe a person too. «Sam sits all day and does not take much exercise, so he is inactive.» Health lessons say that sitting too much is linked to poor fitness, so children are told to move every day.
explain: It can also describe things that are no longer used. «The club's account is inactive, so nobody has logged in for a year.» Check by swapping in a meaning: «The account is not being used» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Inactive means not active; not moving, working or doing anything.
fact: «Physically inactive» means not moving or exercising much.
fact: In science, an inactive volcano is one that is not erupting now.
fact: «Economically inactive» means not working and not looking for work (UK official language).
fact: The opposite of inactive is active.
exercise: «The volcano has been inactive for years.» What does inactive mean here? | Very angry and shouting | Moving very fast | *Not erupting now | Full of water
exercise: Ruby says, «He is inactive because he sits all day.» What does this suggest? | He is very loud and noisy | *He does not take much exercise | He runs every morning before school | He is a famous athlete
exercise: Which word is the opposite of inactive? | Still | Sleepy | *Active | Quiet
test: «The club's account is inactive, so nobody has used it for a year.» What does inactive mean? | Full of money | Very busy with members | Opened every day | *No longer being used
test: What does «physically inactive» describe? | *Someone who does not move or exercise much | A very fast car | Someone who loves football | A volcano that erupts often
exam: Why do health lessons tell children to move every day? | Because inactive people are the best at sport | *Because being inactive is linked to poor fitness | To learn about volcanoes | To stay still for longer
